.\"
.TH "ELEMENT.INPUT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.input_event \- Element: input event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]input\f[B]\f[R] event fires when the \f[CR]value\f[R] of
an \f[CR]<input>\f[R], \f[CR]<select>\f[R], or \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R]
element has been changed as a direct result of a user action (such as
typing in a textbox or checking a checkbox).
.PP
The event also applies to elements with \f[CR]contenteditable\f[R]
enabled, and to any element when \f[CR]designMode\f[R] is turned on.
In the case of \f[CR]contenteditable\f[R] and \f[CR]designMode\f[R], the
event target is the \f[I]editing host\f[R].
If these properties apply to multiple elements, the editing host is the
nearest ancestor element whose parent isn\(cqt editable.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqinput\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
oninput = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
An \f[CR]InputEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]UIEvent\f[R].
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] For \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] and \f[CR]<input>\f[R]
elements that accept text input (\f[CR]type=text\f[R],
\f[CR]type=tel\f[R], etc.), the interface is \f[CR]InputEvent\f[R]; for
others, the interface is \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
For \f[CR]<input>\f[R] elements with \f[CR]type=checkbox\f[R] or
\f[CR]type=radio\f[R], the \f[CR]input\f[R] event should fire whenever a
user toggles the control.
However, historically this has not always been the case.
Check compatibility, or use the \f[CR]change\f[R] event instead for
elements of these types.
.PP
For text controls, the \f[CR]input\f[R] event is fired as the user edits
the value.
This is unlike the \f[CR]change\f[R] event, which only fires when the
value is committed, such as when the control loses focus.
.PP
For \f[CR]<select>\f[R] elements displayed as listboxes (for example,
\f[CR]<select size=\(dq3\(dq>\f[R]), selecting options with the mouse
can change the \f[CR]value\f[R] while the mouse button is still held
down.
The \f[CR]input\f[R] and \f[CR]change\f[R] events are deferred until the
mouse button is released, rather than firing for each intermediate
selection.
If the user drags to another option and back to the original selection
before releasing the button, the selection changes during the drag may
or may not be reported; the behavior diverges between browsers.
.PP
Generally, only user\-initiated value changes, including autofill, are
expected to fire \f[CR]input\f[R].
Some changes to a control\(cqs value do not fire the \f[CR]input\f[R]
event at all, for example:
.IP \(bu 2
Setting the value programmatically, such as by assigning to an
element\(cqs \f[CR]value\f[R] or a \f[CR]<select>\f[R] element\(cqs
\f[CR]selectedIndex\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Changing a control\(cqs child elements in a way that changes its value,
such as removing the selected \f[CR]<option>\f[R] from a
\f[CR]<select>\f[R] element.
.IP \(bu 2
Changing a control\(cqs attributes in a way that causes the browser to
adjust its value, such as changing a range input\(cqs \f[CR]min\f[R] or
\f[CR]max\f[R] so that its current value falls outside the new bounds.
.IP \(bu 2
Resetting a form, which only fires a \f[CR]reset\f[R] event.
.IP \(bu 2
The browser restoring saved form values during history navigation.
Which controls have their values restored can differ between browsers.
.IP \(bu 2
Chrome clearing unedited, autofilled username and password if the
credentials are no longer available, such as when the user signed out of
Chrome after autofilling.
.SH EXAMPLES
This example logs the value whenever you change the value of the
\f[CR]<input>\f[R] element.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]input\f[R] placeholder=\(dqEnter some text\(dq name=\(dqname\(dq />
<\f[B]p\f[R] id=\(dqvalues\(dq></\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] input = document.querySelector(\(dqinput\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.getElementById(\(dqvalues\(dq);

input.addEventListener(\(dqinput\(dq, updateValue);

\f[B]function\f[R] updateValue(e) {
  log.textContent = e.target.value;
}
.EE
.SS Result
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Related events
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]beforeinput\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]change\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]invalid\f[R]
.RE
